(text "POWER INPUT  12 V DC (10 - 18 V, centre +).  ~1 A peak during OCXO warm-up (~1 min), ~0.35 A steady.\nD1 = reverse-polarity diode, F1 = PTC fuse, D5 = TVS.  U6 = L7805CV 12 V -> 5 V (TO-220, 1.5 A).  F1 = radial PTC, 2 A hold.\nU6 HEATSINK REQUIRED: ~8 W during warm-up, ~3 W steady at 13.8 V in.  Use <= 10 C/W or bolt the tab to the case.\nD2 feeds the DevKit VIN and LCD and blocks USB back-feed.  U1 = LD1117V33 (TO-220, 800 mA) for the OCXO only.\nJP6 (fitted by default) links D2 to VIN.  Remove it to program over USB with 12 V applied if the DevKit\nhas no USB VBUS diode (test VBUS->VIN with a meter: ~0.3 V forward = diode present)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15 12 0) (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a580da6e-4122-4013-8166-21890598f54f"))
